> The error bars should show up separately. Maybe I should add a collection of points, each of which will have error bars around them?
**assistant**:
> If you want to display error bars for individual points rather than as part of the line plot or bar plot, you can add a scatter plot with points that include error bars. This way, you can show error bars around each point clearly. Here’s how you can do this in `plotly`:
> 
> ```r
> library(plotly)
> 
> # Sample data
> x <- c(1, 2, 3, 4, 5)
> y_line <- c(10, 15, 13, 17, 14)
> y_bar <- c(5, 7, 6, 8, 5)
> 
> # Error values for each point
> line_error <- c(1, 0.5, 1.2, 0.8, 1)
> bar_error <- c(0.5, 1, 0.2, 0.5, 0.3)
> 
> # Create the line plot
> line_plot <- plot_ly(x = ~x, y = ~y_line, type = 'scatter', mode = 'lines', name = 'Line Plot')
> 
> # Add the bar plot
> bar_plot <- add_bars(line_plot, x = ~x, y = ~y_bar, name = 'Bar Plot')
> 
> # Add points with error bars for the line data
> combined_plot <- bar_plot %>%
>   add_trace(x = ~x, y = ~y_line, type = 'scatter', mode = 'markers', name = 'Line Points',
>             error_y = list(type = 'data', array = line_error, visible = TRUE),
> 
> # Add points with error bars for the bar data
>             error_y = list(type = 'data', array = bar_error, visible = TRUE)) 
> 
> # Show the plot
> combined_plot
> ```
> 
> ### Overview:
> - **Separate Scatter Plot**: By using `add_trace()`, a new scatter plot of points is created, allowing you to specify error bars individually for those points.
>   
> - **Error Bars**: With the `error_y` argument in the scatter plot, you can define `array` containing the error values, which will show up around each point separately.
> 
> ### Customization:
> You can customize the appearance of the points (like size, color, etc.) and error bars as needed. This setup allows for clearer presentation of uncertainty in your data.
> 
> Feel free to modify the code as per your requirements! If you need any more help, I'll be here to assist you!
